					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5045819); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5045819&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200842" alt="Calibri Bold" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5045819)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5045819); return false;" >Calibri Bold</a></span> <span class="odate time_1572016183 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Oct 2019 15:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4406693">
									

<p>First and foremost, thanks to all the people who went over this! <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573401748" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;">Ihp</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/irondruid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4982339); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4982339&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573401748" alt="IronDruid" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4982339)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/irondruid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4982339); return false;">IronDruid</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dyslexion" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5549954); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5549954&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573401748" alt="Dyslexion" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5549954)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dyslexion" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5549954); return false;">Dyslexion</a></span>, you guys were a huge help. And a very special thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gee0765" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5376871); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5376871&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573401748" alt="gee0765" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5376871)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gee0765" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5376871); return false;">gee0765</a></span> for making the ACS header for the Decommissioned class, as well as a big thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5045819); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5045819&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573401748" alt="Calibri Bold" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5045819)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calibri-bold" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5045819); return false;">Calibri Bold</a></span> for designing the Decommissioned icon. To all the rest of you who helped in any way that I have forgotten about, please make yourselves known, or even PM me so that I can put you in the credits list.</p>
<p>Image found <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/22490717@N02/36286967086/">here</a>.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">My&nbsp;reasons&nbsp;for&nbsp;making&nbsp;this.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;hope&nbsp;this&nbsp;provides&nbsp;some&nbsp;clarity.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First, I wanted to use the Decommissioned class, but without any lolFoundation elements. I noticed that Decom. objects could be considered &quot;canon,&quot; and so I wondered what the difference between Decommissioned and Neutralized was in-universe. After some research and talking around, I concluded that Decommissioned objects were intentionally destroyed by the Foundation, while Neutralized ones were objects that were destroyed or deanomalized for any other reason.</p>
<p>Second, I noticed that almost all objects that were destroyed by the Foundation (save for previous Decom. items) were these massive, world-ending forces. I figured that there could conceivably be other reasons to destroy an object, though it would still be done <em>very</em> rarely. What about expense? Would the Foundation spend millions or even billions of dollars to contain an object, even if it had no use to them, and it could be destroyed fairly easily? Or how about legality? The Foundation is still subject to various laws imposed by the governments and entities supporting its existence, so what if the only way to contain an anomaly was in violation of those laws?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

