														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4408532">
									

<p>The initial description is clumsy and uninteresting. I can't really picture how this was stored, and the lack of description of the attacks was a wasted opportunity. I don't really see what the letter adds (e.g., it's a story thread that's just thrown out and never resolved), whereas more description of the attacks throughout history would've added some depth and mental images.</p>
<p>Including the dollar amount seems silly. Precious metals change in value all the time, and &quot;2,500'&lt;unit&gt;s of silver, or gold and gemstomes equivalent in value&quot; or something like that is a much meatier image. If you want to include the dollar amount, I would put that down in the section where they discover the financial link.</p>
<p>The reuse of decommissioning was&#8230; fine. The form was an interesting addition. I don't like the footnote: marking it as a change in policy rather than just a truth in this article's canon feels like an attempt to explain irl site culture in-universe, and I don't really like the stories that leads to (especially if the bar seems low, which having a short form, even if neat, implies). If you just wanted to include a narrative thread about this department being founded, this was a really uninteresting way to do that.</p>
<p>The best ideas in the article were around the temporal/monetary shenanigans. Those were quite good.</p>
<p>No vote.</p>

							</div>

								
