			<div class="content" id="post-content-4421906">
									

<p>A solid article although it's pretty obvious its purpose is to show a case where decommissioning is necessary.</p>
<p>I understand why many might be upset by the precedent this sets- aka articles in the future destroying stuff &quot;because we can&quot; - but it's very clearly shown that this takes place only in exceptional circumstances.</p>
<p>The foundation at this point holds about 5000 scps and although its resources are vast, they aren't infinite (as shown by many other articles). Decommissioning feels like something any real life organisation with these expenses and responsibilities would be forced to do.</p>
<p>+1 for bringing the concept back with a very good example of when it would be necessary</p>

